# +Words, +Budget, -Term
# +Words, +Budget, -Totals
# +Words, -Length
#   * <module> The shortest common superstring: three nested layers, each to be replaced natively
#
# A family of the reduction series: a non-trivial problem with a concise
# definition whose solution needs a pattern recognised and replaced natively
# at every layer of nested subproblems. The problem is LeetCode 943, "Find the Shortest
# Superstring", over bit strings, asking for the length.
#
# The program writes top (corpora/library/top) where the pseudo-code and the
# argument below write {}, the empty choice of the calculus that still has
# it; doc/proofs/reduction_series_answers.md carries the argument over to
# Definition 14, and the generator is the family's Scala object in
# gezi/contest-corpora.
#
# THE PROGRAM, in continuation passing style (a set chosen once, at the head),
# the words let bound once:
#
#     overlaps a b  = { prefix a b (\k. k (length a)) {},  a {} (\h. \rest. overlaps rest b) }
#     tour c p r k  = full c (k r)
#                       { member c i {} (overlaps p w_i (\o.
#                           (\cost. at_least r cost (tour (insert c i) w_i (difference r cost) k) {})
#                             (difference (length w_i) o))) | i a word }
#     program       = tour none nil T (\r. difference T r)
#
# - the inner layer, overlaps, is the set of the lengths of the suffixes of a
#   that are prefixes of b (the attractor bits_prefix); replaced natively it
#   is string matching, the longest overlap by a failure function;
# - the middle layer chooses the next word among those not used, the used
#   words a bit set (bit_set_member, bit_set_insert, bit_set_full); replaced
#   natively it is the dynamic programme over subsets and the last word;
# - the outer layer is the length arithmetic (length, natural_at_least,
#   natural_difference); replaced natively it is integer arithmetic.
# The first word follows the empty word nil, whose only overlap with it is 0.
# The inner layer's members are boxes \k. k o, o an overlap length, as in
# corpora/contest_collect_keys.pl: merging equal boxes by value, read as data
# of a one-constructor Scott type, leaves one member per overlap length.
#
# THE SNAPSHOT. S(P) is the set of the lengths at most T of the strings made
# by writing the words in some order, each overlapping the one before by some
# overlap: superstring_totals/3. The points take T the least such length, the
# shortest superstring's (every order at its longest overlaps), so S(P) is that
# one number; the near miss takes T one less, so S(P) is empty. PROOF, as for
# corpora/contest_collect_keys.pl, with Lemma 2b of
# gezi/doc/proofs/certificate_meta_lemmas.md: (⊇) choose each word's
# branch and, in overlaps, the member of the chosen overlap; (⊆) a pure term
# is reached only through a full bit set, every word once, each cost the
# length of a word less an overlap its predecessor has with it (the members of
# overlaps are boxes of such lengths, bits_prefix and length giving the
# Boolean and the numeral of their definitions), and at_least keeping the
# budget; the term is difference T r, the total length, at most T.
#
# TARGET ALGORITHMS, the specific known algorithms the problem targets, each
# with its prior work:
# - string matching by a failure function: D. E. Knuth, J. H. Morris,
#   V. R. Pratt, Fast Pattern Matching in Strings, SIAM J. Comput. 1977,
#   doi:10.1137/0206024;
# - the dynamic programme over subsets: M. Held, R. M. Karp, A Dynamic
#   Programming Approach to Sequencing Problems, J. SIAM 1962,
#   doi:10.1137/0110015.
#
# READINGS AND SIZES: in the points' comment below (THE POINTS).
# LIMITS: the reduction family's, 10 s, 256 MB, 256 MB.

#   THE POINTS: superstring_point(?Point, ?Count, ?Length, ?Slack), Count
#   words of Length bits from a linear congruential sequence (seed 7), the
#   budget the shortest superstring's length plus Slack. Sized by a
#   probe of 2026-09-30 (CPUs 0-7, the whole set under a 10 s limit,
#   the budget the least length): tabling(weak_head) reads four words of 6
#   bits in 369 ms, five in 1854 ms and six of 8 bits in 3147 ms, and is
#   stopped at seven words of 8 bits; weak_head reads four words of 6 bits
#   in 2628 ms. The near miss takes the budget one short.
#
# Each text is from_cbor of a string literal, a Scott list of bytes,
# imported from corpora/library/text/cbor. Each number is from_cbor of an
# integer literal, a Scott integer, imported from corpora/library/integer/cbor.
# FIXME: the imports project "corpora" https://github.com/Atry/private-overlay/issues/1923
# off the variable gezi, the name of the project root's own
# directory; it breaks if that directory is renamed.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "list")
λ nil cons _ _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "text") "cbor")
λ text_from_cbor _ _ _
. (λtuple. tuple λ. text_from_cbor λx. x)
λ text
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "integer") "cbor")
λ integer_from_cbor _
. (λtuple. tuple λ. integer_from_cbor λx. x)
λ integer
